    {
      "h2": "Postal code or ZIP code",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "p": "ZIP code is the United States term. Canada's equivalent is the postal code, and it mixes letters and digits where a ZIP code is digits only. A five-digit number is not a Canadian postal code."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "h2": "Why it matters for postage",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "p": "Canada Post's price guide says an item with a missing or incorrect postal code must be paid at the other Lettermail prices, which start at $2.61 instead of $1.24 to $1.44. Canada Post also provides a free postal code lookup on its website. See [how to address a letter to Canada](/blog/how-to-address-a-letter-to-canada) for where the code goes."
        }
      ]
    }
